# Sources other than Wikipedia for the Joan of Arc story. Run: ./node_modules/.bin/harita sources joan-of-arc
# An address the command cannot fetch can be saved from a browser under the name the command prints.

# The trials (primary)
https://sourcebooks.web.fordham.edu/basis/joanofarc-trial.asp  # The Trial of Jeanne d'Arc, tr. W. P. Barrett 1932, Fordham Internet History Sourcebooks: the trial of condemnation, 1431, in full
https://archive.org/download/jeannedarcmaidof028754mbp/jeannedarcmaidof028754mbp_djvu.txt  # T. Douglas Murray (ed. and tr.), Jeanne d'Arc, Maid of Orleans, 1902: both trials in English, the depositions of 1455-1456
https://sourcebooks.web.fordham.edu/halsall/source/joanofarc.asp  # Joan's letter to the English, March 1429, Fordham Medieval Sourcebook
https://archive.org/download/procsdecondam04joanuoft/procsdecondam04joanuoft_djvu.txt  # J. Quicherat (ed.), Procès de condamnation et de réhabilitation, vol. 4, 1847: the chronicles, the Journal du siège d'Orléans, Berry, Chartier, Monstrelet
https://archive.org/download/ProcesDeCondamnationV5/ProcesDeCondamnationV5_djvu.txt  # J. Quicherat (ed.), Procès, vol. 5, 1849: letters, accounts and documents of her life

# Chronicles (primary)
https://archive.org/download/chroniquesdeperc00cagnuoft/chroniquesdeperc00cagnuoft_djvu.txt  # Perceval de Cagny, Chroniques, ed. H. Moranvillé 1902: Alençon's household, 1429-1430
https://archive.org/download/chroniquedelapuc00cousuoft/chroniquedelapuc00cousuoft_djvu.txt  # Chronique de la Pucelle (Cousinot), ed. A. Vallet de Viriville 1859
https://archive.org/download/journaldunbourge54182gut/54182-0.txt  # Journal d'un bourgeois de Paris 1405-1449, ed. A. Tuetey 1881: Paris under the Burgundians and the English
https://archive.org/download/chroniclesengue06johngoog/chroniclesengue06johngoog_djvu.txt  # Monstrelet, Chronicles, tr. T. Johnes, Bohn 1849, the volume of books 1-2 to 1435: Orléans 1407, Agincourt, Montereau, Verneuil, the Herrings, the Maid, Compiègne
https://archive.org/download/chroniclesengue07johngoog/chroniclesengue07johngoog_djvu.txt  # Monstrelet, Chronicles, tr. T. Johnes, Bohn 1849, the volume of book 2 from 1435, book 3 and the continuation: Arras, Paris 1436, Formigny, Castillon
https://archive.org/download/henriciquintian00willgoog/henriciquintian00willgoog_djvu.txt  # Henrici Quinti gesta, ed. and tr. B. Williams 1850: the chaplain's account of Harfleur and Agincourt

https://www.vatican.va/archive/aas/documents/AAS-12-1920-ocr.pdf  # Acta Apostolicae Sedis 12, 1920: the bull Divina disponente of Benedict XV, her canonisation

# Modern works (scholarly)
https://archive.org/download/lancasterandyor00ramsgoog/lancasterandyor00ramsgoog_djvu.txt  # J. H. Ramsay, Lancaster and York, vol. 1, Oxford, Clarendon Press 1892: Henry V, Verneuil, Orléans, the Maid
https://archive.org/download/cu31924088011436/cu31924088011436_djvu.txt  # J. H. Ramsay, Lancaster and York, vol. 2, Oxford, Clarendon Press 1892: Arras, Normandy lost, Formigny, Castillon
https://archive.org/download/reignofhenryfift02wyliuoft/reignofhenryfift02wyliuoft_djvu.txt  # J. H. Wylie, The Reign of Henry the Fifth, vol. 2, Cambridge UP 1919: Harfleur and Agincourt
https://archive.org/download/reignofhenryfift03wyliuoft/reignofhenryfift03wyliuoft_djvu.txt  # J. H. Wylie and W. T. Waugh, The Reign of Henry the Fifth, vol. 3, Cambridge UP 1929: Normandy, Montereau, Troyes
https://archive.org/download/historyofartofwa0002char/historyofartofwa0002char_djvu.txt  # C. Oman, A History of the Art of War in the Middle Ages, vol. 2, 1924: Agincourt, Verneuil, Patay, Formigny, Castillon
https://archive.org/download/joanofarc00lowe/joanofarc00lowe_djvu.txt  # F. C. Lowell, Joan of Arc, Boston 1896: her life from the sources, with notes
https://archive.org/download/maidoffrancebein00languoft/maidoffrancebein00languoft_djvu.txt  # A. Lang, The Maid of France, 1909: her life from Quicherat, with notes
https://archive.org/download/thelifeofjoanofa19488gut/19488.txt  # A. France, The Life of Joan of Arc, tr. W. Stephens 1909: with notes
https://archive.org/download/beaucourt-histoire-de-charles-vii-v-1/Beaucourt%20Histoire%20de%20Charles%20VII%20v%201_djvu.txt  # G. du Fresne de Beaucourt, Histoire de Charles VII, vol. 1, 1881: the Dauphin to 1422
https://archive.org/download/beaucourt-histoire-de-charles-vii-v-2/Beaucourt%20Histoire%20de%20Charles%20VII%20v%202_djvu.txt  # Beaucourt, Histoire de Charles VII, vol. 2, 1882: the King of Bourges, 1422-1435
https://archive.org/download/beaucourt-histoire-de-charles-vii-v-5/Beaucourt%20Histoire%20de%20Charles%20VII%20v%205_djvu.txt  # Beaucourt, Histoire de Charles VII, vol. 5, 1890: the conquest of Normandy and Guyenne, 1449-1453
https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/08409c.htm  # H. Thurston, St. Joan of Arc, Catholic Encyclopedia 1910, signed: her life, the rehabilitation, the beatification
https://academie1744-rouen.fr/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/La-canonisation-de-Jeanne-dArc.pdf  # C. Renoux, La canonisation de Jeanne d'Arc, Académie de Rouen colloquium 2022: the process of 1869 to 1920

# Unread: these sites answer a script with a bot wall (Anubis), which the command takes for the page.
# Save each from a browser as .references/<name the command gives>.html, then take the "# " off its line and run the command.
# https://books.openedition.org/puc/7802  # Presses universitaires de Caen: the two trials of Joan of Arc, 1431 and 1456
